  "work": {
    "abstract_text": "We prove Paul Barry's shifted Hankel conjecture in OEIS A188475, revision 2 (April 1, 2011): for every n>=0, det[q(i+j+2)]_(0<=i,j<=n)=(2n^3+3n^2+n+3)/3, by a moment-matrix cofactor argument extending Cigler's unit-descent formula (2011, Theorem A*). The same calculation gives both adjacent shifts and a parameter formula det[q_lambda(i+j+2)]_(i,j<N)=1+lambda*sum(k^2,k=0..N-1) for every complex lambda, with q_lambda defined by its Catalan generating function. A direct bijection relates the source's nonexchangeable subsequences to Callan's restricted Grand Dyck paths.",
